<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conques</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conques is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aveyron">Aveyron</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the Rouergue hills. Its abbey church of Sainte-Foy, a major stop on the pilgrim route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Santiago de Compostela</a>, holds the relics of Saint Faith and a famous gold reliquary statue of the saint. The church's carved tympanum of the Last Judgement is one of the masterpieces of Romanesque sculpture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conques.jpg" alt="Conques" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guimsou · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbatiale_de_Conques_et_la_ville.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
